course.json is derived from two files of the Electronic Dictionary Research
and Development Group (EDRDG):

- KANJIDIC2 (https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project):
  meanings, readings, school grade, frequency and stroke count.
- KRADFILE (https://www.edrdg.org/krad/kradinf.html): the components each
  kanji is made of.

Both are used in conformance with the Group's licence
(https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html), which applies the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence:
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

course.json is a derivative work (kanji reordered into levels, components
reduced to the direct parts of each kanji, and component names added) and is
distributed under the same licence. The rest of this repository is not covered
by this notice.
